                "event": "Flood Advisory",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Fort Worth TX",
                "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 3 at 3:56PM CDT until October 3 at 7:30PM CDT by NWS Fort Worth TX",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Henderson County in central Texas...\nEastern Navarro County in north central Texas...\n\n* WHEN...Until 730 PM CDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nOverflowing poor drainage areas. Some low-water crossings may\nbecome impassable.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 354 PM CDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Overflowing poor drainage areas will cause minor\nflooding in the advisory area.\n- A Flash Flood Warning remains in effect for the city of Athens\nthrough 6 PM CDT. Please see the warning bulletin for more\ninformation.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nCorsicana, Athens, Gun Barrel City, Mabank, Malakoff, Tool,\nKerens, Seven Points, Eustace, Trinidad, Angus, Enchanted Oaks,\nCaney City, Navarro, Trinidad Lake, Forest Grove Reservoir, Cedar\nCreek Reservoir, Flag Lake, Purtis Creek State Park and\nRichland-Chambers Reservoir.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
